strong> (95% range +0.18 to +0.30), about +3.1\u00b0F since 1894. Orlando's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.07\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.01 to +0.13), about +0.9\u00b0F since 1894.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 11 of 12 months. Highs rose in 4 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Orlando's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.13 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 51.4 inches a year. The wettest year was 1905 (74.79 in); the driest, 2000 (30.38 in). Orlando almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.0 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 9 daily record highs, 2 daily record lows"}}